  <input id="angleErrorInput" type="range" min="0" max="2" step="0.05" value="0" oninput="document.getElementById('angleErrorVal').value=this.value;update_angleError(+this.value)"></label>
<span style="display:block;color:#666;line-height:1.4;margin-top:2px">Angles alone never give a distance — you always need one <i>known length</i>: a height h or a baseline t. The sketch is exaggerated for clarity; the small inset in the readout shows the <i>true</i> proportions. Click the eye, the stations, the boat or the orange wedge.</span>
